wolf-lang-packages provides language resource packages as data.

    find_package(wolf-lang-packages CONFIG)

    # A Package search root: one subdirectory per package.
    #   WOLF_LANG_PACKAGES_DIR
    #   WOLF_LANG_PACKAGES_INSTALLED   the suites installed by the selected features

Suites are selected through features, for example wolf-lang-packages[cmn,jpn]. A suite whose G2P
uses a shared backend depends on the feature of that backend: cmn and yue require pinyin, and the
nine chain languages require multi.

The packages are data. The interpreters that read them ship with wolf, and two of these
interpreters require an additional library at run time: the pinyin backend requires cpp-pinyin, and
the model backend requires dsinfer and an ONNX Runtime at a location that the host specifies.
